# NYBOSS .NET Developer

You are working on the NYBOSS .NET server repository.

Follow the NYBOSS project creation rules in this skill and its reference files.

## Current Scope

The current automation phase focuses ONLY on creating .NET projects.

Do not generate the internal application contents such as:
- Controllers
- Models
- Interfaces
- Service classes
- Repository classes
- Business logic
- Message handlers
- Dependency injection registrations

unless the user explicitly requests them.

## Project Creation

When the user asks to create a new project, determine the required project composition using these rules.

### 1. Simple/default project

If the user asks for:
- a simple project
- a basic project
- a normal project
- a standard project
- a project without specifying its structure

use the default NYBOSS Business project composition:

- API
- Common
- Repository
- Services

Example:

Customer

becomes:

Customer.API
Customer.Common
Customer.Repository
Customer.Services

### 2. Explicit project composition

If the user explicitly specifies project components, create only those components.

Example:

"Create Customer with Common, Repository and Services"

creates:

Customer.Common
Customer.Repository
Customer.Services

Do not add API unless requested.

### 3. Similar to an existing project

If the user says:

"Create Customer similar to ManualForecast"

inspect the existing ManualForecast project structure and determine which project components it contains.

Use that structure as the reference for the new project.

The existing project's naming convention must NOT be copied.

For example:

ManualForecast.API

becomes:

Customer.API

not:

BNPP.NYBOSS.Customer.API

Existing projects are used as structural references only.

## Naming Convention

All newly created projects must use:

<ProjectName>.<Component>

Examples:

Customer.API
Customer.Common
Customer.Repository
Customer.Services

Do NOT add the legacy `BNPP.NYBOSS` prefix to newly generated project names.

Existing project names must not determine the naming convention of newly created projects.

## Project References

During project creation:

- Add only the basic references required between the newly created project components.
- Do NOT copy all ProjectReference entries from an existing project.
- Do NOT add references to unrelated existing NYBOSS projects automatically.
- Do NOT add Infrastructure, Gateway, Core, or other external project references unless explicitly required by the user's request or the selected project pattern.

External project references will be handled separately when the user requests them.

## Solution

New projects must be added to the existing NYBOSS solution:

BNPP.NYBOSS.NextGen.Server.sln

Do not create a new solution for an application.

## .NET CLI

Use the .NET CLI for project creation and solution operations.

Use the appropriate `dotnet new` template for the requested project type.

Use:

dotnet sln <solution> add <project>

to add newly created projects to the existing solution.

Use:

dotnet add <project> reference <referenced-project>

only when a project-to-project reference is required.

## Important

Before creating a project similar to an existing NYBOSS project, inspect the existing project structure and its project file.

Use the existing project to understand structure and purpose.

Do not blindly copy its:
- project name
- assembly name
- root namespace
- project references
- package references
- business-specific configuration

The generated project must follow the new naming convention defined above.

